ico, with the government seeking to hold these companies liable for the harm caused by smuggled guns.\n  - id: 24-924, name: Hencely v. Fluor Corp., description: The case Hencely v. Fluor Corp. centers on whether a soldier injured by contractor negligence can pursue claims against the company, with Fluor arguing that constitutional and federal interests preempt such claims.\n  - id: 25-1083, name: Mullin, Sec. of Homeland Security v. Doe, description: The case concerns the Secretary\'s decision to terminate temporary protected status for Syria and Haiti, with petitioners seeking judicial review of this action but the government arguing that a specific provision bars such review.\n  - id: 23-713, name: Bufkin v. McDonough, Sec. of VA, description: The case is about whether the Veterans Court should review the Department of Veterans Affairs\' decisions under a more generous standard, as required by Congress, or continue to review them under a less generous standard.\n  - id: 21-234, name: George v. McDonough, description: The case George v. McDonough, docket number 21-234, concerns the veterans benefits system and whether a government agency\'s regulation can override a clear legal error in a decision, potentially depriving veterans of their rightful benefits.\n  - id: 20-480, name: Babcock v. Kijakazi, description: The case concerns whether a former National Guard technician who served for 33 years qualifies for an exemption from the windfall elimination provision, with the government arguing that his service was not as a member of a uniformed service.\n  - id: 20-603, name: Torres v. Texas Dept. of Public Safety, description: The Constitution granted Congress the power to raise and support Armies, which includes authorizing lawsuits against states, to ensure national survival. This power is unique and essential for the federal government\'s preeminent national defense function, particularly in light of modern military needs and USERRA protections.\n  - id: 21-1454, name: OH Adjutant Gen.\'s Dept. v. FLRA, description: The case is about whether the Federal Labor Relations Authority has the power to issue orders to state guards and adjutants general, who employ technicians, or if they are exempt from the Authority\'s jurisdiction under a federal law known as the Reform Act.\n  - id: 22-888, name: Rudisill v. McDonough, Sec. of VA, description: The case concerns a veteran\'s entitlement to wartime benefits under the Post-9/11 GI Bill, specifically whether they can claim those benefits without first using up or exhausting their peacetime Montgomery benefits.\n  - id: 24-20, name: Fuld v. PLO, description: The case Fuld v. PLO concerns whether the federal government can bring a civil action against organizations responsible for terror activity abroad that kills American citizens, despite their claims that it violates due process rights.\n  - id: 19-177, name: Agency for Int’l Development v. Alliance for Open Society Int’l, Inc., description: The case is about whether the US government can require foreign organizations receiving AIDS relief funding to have a policy opposing prostitution and sex trafficking, despite the Supreme Court previously ruling that this condition cannot be applied to domestic organizations.\n  - id: 23-21, name: Harrow v. Dept. of Defense, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether a specific filing deadline in the Harrow v. Dept. of Defense case is a procedural rule or a requirement for the court\'s jurisdiction, with implications for how appeals are handled.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
